---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Submission privacy notice — Nick’s Media"
  description="How Nick’s Media handles editorial report submissions — what we collect, why we collect it, how long we keep it, and your choices."
>
<article class="legal section-pad">
        <div class="section-label">
          <span>Privacy</span> Submission privacy notice
        </div>
        <h1>How we handle <em>your report.</em></h1>
        <p class="legal-intro">
          This notice explains what happens when you send a report, story pitch,
          or tip to the Nick’s Media newsroom through the report form on our
          site. Please read it before you submit. You must agree to it before
          the form will send anything.
        </p>

        <section>
          <h2>What we collect</h2>
          <p>
            When you submit through the report form we collect only what you
            provide:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Your name (as you give it).</li>
            <li>Your email address, so an editor can follow up.</li>
            <li>The desk you selected.</li>
            <li>Your headline and the details of the report.</li>
            <li>
              The date and time of your consent, and a link to this notice.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We do not require an account, and we do not collect payment or
            government identifiers through this form.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
          <p>
            We use your submission to evaluate and, where appropriate, verify
            and report on the story. Your contact details are used to reach you
            for follow-up questions and to confirm details. We do not sell
            submissions or use them for advertising.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
          <p>
            Submissions are retained for a limited period for editorial review
            and then deleted automatically. We keep them only as long as needed
            to consider and, if verified, report the story, or as required by
            law. Ask us and we will tell you the current retention period.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Who can see it</h2>
          <p>
            Access is limited to Nick’s Media editors who need it to review and
            verify the story. We do not publish your identity or contact details
            without your agreement, unless the law requires it. Reports are
            treated as unverified tips and are checked independently before
            anything is published.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Before you submit</h2>
          <p>
            <strong
              >Do not send confidential or urgent information through this
              page.</strong
            >
            Anything you submit may not be monitored around the clock. If your
            material is sensitive, illegal to hold, or involves immediate risk
            to someone’s safety, contact the newsroom through the published
            contact email first and wait for guidance.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Your choices</h2>
          <p>
            You can ask us to access, correct, or delete a submission you have
            sent, and you can withdraw your consent for future handling. To make
            a request, email
            <a
              href="mailto:hello@nicksmedia.com?subject=Submission%20privacy%20request"
              >hello@nicksmedia.com</a
            >
            with enough detail for us to find your submission. Requests may be
            limited where the law, or the need to verify a live story, requires
            us to keep certain records.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section>
          <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this notice as our newsroom and the law change. The
            current version will always be published at this address, and the
            date of the latest revision is shown below.
          </p>
        </section>

        <p class="legal-updated">
          Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-11">11 October 2026</time>.
        </p>

        <p class="legal-actions">
          <a class="button button-dark" href="index.html#live"
            >Back to the report desk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
          >
        </p>
      </article>
</BaseLayout>
